  "overview": "<p><strong>Universidad de Monterrey</strong>, acronym <strong>\"UDEM\"</strong>, is a private Catholic-inspired educational institution, open to all creeds and conditions, founded in 1969.</p><p>The UDEM Campus is located in the municipality of San Pedro Garza Garcia belonging to the <strong>Metropolitan Area of </strong>Monterrey, Nuevo Leon, Mexico.</p><p>It is home to about <strong>16,000 students</strong>, primarily in undergraduate programs. The campus is nestled in the mountains, just outside of the city of Monterrey.</p><p>UDEM was founded by the <strong>Daughters of the Immaculate Mary of Guadalupe</strong>, the <strong>nuns of the Sacred Heart</strong>, the Marist Brothers, and the La Salle<strong> members</strong>, supported by an association of Catholic citizens.</p><p>The idea originated from a recommendation given by the <strong>Second Vatican Council</strong> to use educational activities in favor of teaching the principles of the Catholic doctrine.</p>",
  "administrative": "<p><strong>1. Application Dossier</strong></p><p>You will work directly with the partner university regarding your application.</p><p>All required documents will have to be uploaded on their platform or sent by email before the deadline (see the <strong>Americas Teams channel</strong> for each application deadline).</p><p>If you have not received anything yet, it means your nomination has not been sent yet — please be patient.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>In the past, the partner has asked for the following:</strong></p><ul><li>Two recommendation letters from professors</li><li>Proof of health insurance coverage</li><li>Course request list</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>To be given to Epitech bachelor campus administration to reenroll for the Tech4 (in April/May):</strong></p><ul><li>The addendum to the contract</li><li>EPITECH re-registration dossier</li></ul><p><br></p><p>This information is <strong>subject to change</strong> by the partner university. They will provide you with the most current information upon your acceptance.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Visa</strong></p><p><strong>In France: student Student Temporary Resident Visa</strong> (more information <a href=\"https://consulmex.sre.gob.mx/leamington/index.php/non-mexicans/visas/117-student-visa\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>and <a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/en/admisiones-y-becas/tramites-migratorios\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)</p><p>Once you receive the acceptance letter from the partner university, you will be able to apply for a visa. Please refer to the <strong>Mexican Embassy or Consulate</strong> closer to you to ensure you have the proper documentation before arriving in Mexico.</p><p><br></p><p><u>General requirements:</u></p><ul><li>Original passport that is valid for at least three months longer than your intended stay in Mexico. Photocopies of the main pages (personal data, expiration date, and photograph).</li><li>Visa application form, duly completed and bearing your signature. The application form is available at the website of the corresponding embassy or consulate.</li><li>Acceptance letter from UDEM. Sometimes you will be asked to submit a photocopy and sometimes they will keep the original document. Because of this, we suggest that you always keep a copy.</li><li>You must prove financial solvency and that you can provide yourself with at least <strong>USD$300 per month</strong>.</li><li>If the holders of the bank account that you will be using for proof of financial solvency are your parents, you must submit the banking certificate and a <strong>letter of promise from your parents</strong> in which they pledge to support you financially during the duration of your stay in Mexico. If you have a scholarship, you must submit a letter of proof that includes the amount of your scholarship.</li><li>Photographs (the format and number vary in each embassy and consulate).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Arrival in Mexico: Residence Card </strong>(more information <a href=\"https://www.inm.gob.mx/mpublic/publico/inm-tramites.html?a=thgeGuQHx2k%3D&amp;tr=hyBh72VpD1w%3D&amp;h_sdp00=giUnJ9XgtISVcdYJXduIGw%3D%3D\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>and <a href=\"https://www.inm.gob.mx/tramites/publico/solicitud_estancia.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)</p><p>Your pre-approved visa is valid for entry into Mexico only 1 time and you must enter Mexico within 180 days of issuance. Once in Mexico you have 30 days to apply to your local National Migration Institute (INM) for the residence card that accredits their legal stay in the country and allows them to remain in Mexico.</p><p><br></p><p><u>Notes:</u></p><ul><li>The process must be carried out in the city of your campus.</li><li>The INM closes at 1:00 p.m. We recommend that you arrive on time for your appointment.</li><li>Make the appointment as soon as you arrive to Mexico, because sometimes the waiting time may exceed the 30 days you have to make this process.</li><li>Write exactly the full names and surnames with which the person is being identified foreigner in the processing request. (Regardless of the number of names and surnames).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>3. Insurance and Health</strong></p><p>It is imperative that you take out <strong>an international insurance </strong>that will cover you for your medical and hospital expenses, repatriation and accompanied by civil liability. International insurance must cover the entire period of your studies in the country. Insurance costs are the responsibility of each student.&nbsp;</p><p>To take out international insurance, the market is quite open. Please click <a href=\"https://epitech.globalcampus.app/page/international-insurance/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"><u>here </u></a>for more information.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>For more information, you can consult the country's health file at: <a href=\"https://www.pasteur.fr/fr/centre-medical/preparer-son-voyage/mexique\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.pasteur.fr/fr/centre-medical/preparer-son-voyage/mexique</a></p><p><br></p><p>Note: It is advisable to register on the French register established outside of France and to report to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs via the Ariane platform: <a href=\"https://pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fildariane/dyn/public/login.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://pastel.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fildariane/dyn/public/login.html</a></p><p><br></p><p><strong>4.Prepare your arrival</strong></p><p>For advice to travelers issued by the Ministry of Europe and Foreign Affairs on Mexico, click <a href=\"https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/conseils-aux-voyageurs/conseils-par-pays-destination/mexique/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>5.Campus Life</strong></p><p>Facilities include: a library, a bookstore, computer labs, workshops, a cafeteria, coffee shops, a gymnasium, football and tennis courts, banks, a medical clinic, etc.</p>",
  "accomodation": "<p><strong>On-campus accommodation</strong> (more information <a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/en/vive/residencias-udem\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)</p><p>UDEM has residence halls with shared rooms (2 people per room). Food is not included.</p><p>Rooms are furnished with all the amenities: air conditioning, first-rate furniture, WiFi, weekly cleaning service. There are also common areas, which are equipped with screens, sofas and couches; common rooms with football and pool tables, a kitchen area, chimneys, grill. There are also exclusive areas for residents, like the gym, the computer room and Deck.</p><p>Costs in Fall 2025: 83000$MXN (3850€)/ per semester.</p><p>You can contact residencias@udem.edu.mx for additional information.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Off-campus accommodation</strong> (more information <a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/en/vive/buscohogar\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>)</p><p>Options include shared apartments with roommates or private accommodation.</p><p>At <em>Buscohogar</em> (Housing Locator) we provide out-of-town and foreign UDEM students, faculty, and collaborators with information and support on matters related to their search for housing options in Monterrey.</p><p>Costs for housing off-campus: 350-650€.</p><p>You can contact buscohogar@udem.edu.mx for additional information.</p><p>You can also check out off-campus accommodation by yourself through websites like <a href=\"https://www.vivanuncios.com.mx/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Vivanuncios.</a></p>",
  "courses": "<p><strong>Credits</strong></p><p><strong>Number of local credits to be earned per year:</strong> 72 (approximately 36 per semester).</p><p>Students must take <strong>36 credits per semester</strong> in order to obtain <strong>60 ECTS for the year</strong>.</p><p>Courses are worth <strong>6 Mexican credits</strong> each</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Academic Calendar</strong></p><p>Fall semester: Early August - Early December</p><p>Spring semester: Mid January - Late May</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Department and Courses</strong></p><p>Students may take courses from one of the following programs in Engineering and Technologies:</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/en/engineering-and-technologies/programs/electronic-technologies-and-robotics-engineering#syllabus\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Electronic Technology and Robotics</a> (3rd year courses or higher)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/en/engineering-and-technologies/programs/bachelor-computer-science-and-technology\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Computer Science</a> (3rd year courses or higher)</li></ul><p>Some <strong>Computer Science</strong>, <strong>Engineering</strong>, <strong>Graphic Design</strong>, and <strong>Business</strong> courses are available in English.</p><p>You can see the <a href=\"https://www.udem.edu.mx/sites/default/files/2022-06/Courses-in-English-Fall-2022.pdf\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">English courses available</a> on UDEM’s website, but keep in mind that these could change from year to year. Students may also take <strong>beginner courses</strong> in <strong>business</strong>, <strong>finance</strong>, <strong>economics</strong>, etc.</p><p>It is possible to take courses in <strong>English</strong> and in <strong>Spanish</strong>. However, the choice of courses in English is <strong>somewhat limited</strong>.</p><p>If you are interested in taking courses in Spanish, you must have at least a <strong>B1 level</strong>, which will be checked by the partner university via a <strong>Spanish proficiency test during orientation</strong>.</p><p><strong>Course Format and Workload</strong></p><p>Courses includes additional independent work (practical work, tutorials, fieldwork, homework, individual study, and other assessment activities)</p><p>The grading system is the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Maximum grade:</strong> 100</li><li><strong>Passing grade:</strong> 70</li><li><strong>Failed course:</strong> 69 or less</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Important Notes</strong></p><ul><li>Presence in class is <strong>compulsory</strong>, under penalty of <strong>loss of visa and repatriation to France at the student's expense</strong> (impact on credits).</li><li>The courses are most likely <strong>more academic than at EPITECH</strong>.</li><li>The course list is given for information only. It can change from year to year.</li><li>If a course is not available when you arrive on site, <strong>EPITECH cannot be held responsible for it</strong>.</li><li>Any Tech 4 abroad involves an <strong>EIP</strong>! Take advantage of the free slots you will have to advance it.</li></ul>",
  "cost": "<p><strong>Financial Overview (4th Year EPITECH)</strong></p><ul><li>You must pay the <strong>tuition fees for the 4th year of EPITECH</strong>, as well as the <strong>re-registration fees and related fees</strong>.</li><li>EPITECH covers the <strong>application fees</strong> and <strong>part of the tuition fees</strong>.</li><li>The <strong>tuition supplement payable by you</strong> is indicated at the top of this page (if applicable).</li><li>Other costs at your expense include: <strong>travel, accommodation on site, insurance, and everyday expenses</strong> (books, food, transport, etc.).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Other Expenses</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Roundtrip flights:</strong> about 1000€ depending on the airline &amp; travel dates</li><li><strong>Insurance: </strong>300-600€ depending on the company and the coverage</li><li><strong>Visa</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Estimated monthly budget</strong></p><p>The local currency is the <strong>Mexican Peso</strong>. <strong>1 € = 21.48MXN </strong>(rate as of <strong>October 2025).</strong></p><p>Please check the <a href=\"https://fr.numbeo.com/co%C3%BBt-de-la-vie/ville/Monterrey\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Numbeo </a>website to <strong>compare the cost of living between your city of origin and your city of exchange. </strong>Please note that everyone's budget will be different according to one's lifestyle.</p><p>The cost of living in Monterrey is between $600 and $800 USD per month considering: housing, food and other activities.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\"></p><p><br></p><p>These prices are indicative and may vary.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Information (specifics, advice, useful links, etc.)</strong></p><ul><li>Monterrey is hot! From May to August, temperatures can reach 40 degrees or more. It is highly recommended that you move into a flat with air conditioning.</li></ul>",
